  "explanation": "Air trapping from a suspected inhaled foreign body is best confirmed with inspiratory and expiratory chest radiographs, which may show unilateral hyperinflation on expiration. Bronchoscopy is the definitive diagnostic and therapeutic procedure, but the question asks specifically for confirmation of air trapping.",
